      "side": 1,
      "message": "For boards using `CONFIG_BATTERY_PRESENT_CUSTOM`, the `battery_set_cached_presence` update based on battery responsiveness at the bottom of this function is compiled out.\n\nSince `init_battery_type()` sets the cached presence to `BP_YES` (or `BP_NO`) on initialization, and custom `battery_is_present()` implementations (like in lapis/hekla) now return the cached value unconditionally if it\u0027s not `BP_NOT_SURE`, the cached presence will never revert to `BP_NOT_SURE` upon a battery disconnect. This locks the battery presence state permanently to its initial value.\n\nYou should consider moving the `battery_set_cached_presence` update outside the `#if` block or rethinking how custom boards clear the cache on disconnect.",
